{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-127137",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The osculating plane passes through the point $P$, which is at the tip of the vector $r(0).$ The vectors $T(0)$ and $N(0)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, a parametric equation for the plane can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(0)+s\\,T(0)+u\\,N(0),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{0}^{3},\\,2-{0}^{2},\\,0⟩=⟨0,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, a parametric equation for the osculating plane at the point $(0,2,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(0)+s\\,T(0)+u\\,N(0) \\\\  & =⟨0,2,0⟩+s⟨0,0,1⟩+u⟨0,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2-u,\\,s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
